## At home

- use **good, bright lighting** aimed at what you are doing
- use high contrast, such as a dark chopping board for light foods
- use large print, talking books and bump-on dots for dials

## Technology

Phones, tablets and computers can **enlarge text** or **read it aloud**. Voice assistants can help with calls, reminders and questions.

## Stop smoking

Stopping smoking is the most important thing you can do to protect your sight.

## Driving

You must tell the **DVLA** if you have AMD in **both eyes** (or in either eye if you drive a lorry or bus). You must stop driving if you cannot meet the eyesight standard.

## Your feelings

Losing sight can be very upsetting. It is normal to feel low or anxious. Support groups and talking therapies can help.

## Support

The **Macular Society** and **RNIB** both run free helplines and support services.
